DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The hhuubb node type provides a simple mechanism for distributing packets
     over several links.  Packets received on any of the hooks are forwarded
     out the other hooks.  Packets are not altered in any way.

HHOOOOKKSS
     A hhuubb node accepts any request to connect, regardless of the hook name,
     as long as the name is unique.

CCOONNTTRROOLL MMEESSSSAAGGEESS
     This node type supports the generic control messages, plus the following:

     NGM_HUB_SET_PERSISTENT (sseettppeerrssiisstteenntt)
          This command sets the persistent flag on the node, and takes no ar‐
          guments.

SSHHUUTTDDOOWWNN
     This node shuts down upon receipt of a NGM_SHUTDOWN control message, or
     when all hooks have been disconnected.  Setting the persistent flag via a
     NGM_HUB_SET_PERSISTENT control message disables automatic node shutdown
     when the last hook gets disconnected.

